# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-context exclusions. This file is what keeps host-side build artifacts
# (.next, node_modules, .git) OUT of the image — without it, `COPY . .` drags
# a stale local `.next`/`node_modules` into the build and reproduces exactly
# the "latest commit but old output" bug.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies & build output — always rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
.next
out
build

# Version control / CI — never needed at build time.
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Local env & secrets. Only `.env.example` (no secrets) may be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs & debug artifacts.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# Docker files themselves are not part of the build context.
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Docs & tooling not required to build or run the site.
README.md
AGENTS.md
*.md
.vscode
.idea

# TypeScript incremental build cache / Next env stub (regenerated on build).
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# OS cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
